{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_transport",
  "description": "Stage-2 implementation of the pointwise slice of the CISM thickness/tracer solve (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00_002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch, reference run T1850Gg/f09_g17_gris20; CISM_LANE.md rows 6/7/14): the parts of glissade_thickness_tracer_solve that are not horizontal/vertical grid operations. (a) GladSmb - the cap qsmb-to-acab conversion and the glad-level zeroing (libglad/glad_main.F90:810-824, libglad/glad_timestep.F90:171-200): the Fortran chain acab = qsmb*tstep_mbal*hours2seconds/rhow*rhow/rhoi*windows_per_year with the named glad/glimmer constants hours2seconds = 3600 s/h (glad_constants.F90:44), rhow = SHR_CONST_RHOFW = 1000 kg/m3 and rhoi = SHR_CONST_RHOICE = 917 kg/m3 (glimmer_physcon.F90:41-43) and scyr = 31536000 s/yr (glimmer_physcon.F90:90) driving the DERIVED windows_per_year = scyr/(tstep_mbal*hours2seconds) [1/yr; = 1 in the reference run, tstep_mbal = 8760 h = 1 yr; the Fortran's per-window accumulation m w.e., converted to m/yr ice], then acab = 0 where thck <= 0 and acab < 0 (ice-free ablation) and where the cell is ice-free ocean (the cism_ocean predicate: topg < eus and no ice, glide_mask.inc:33-34). The further cap 'acab = -thck_temp' of glad_timestep.F90:233-235 is applied AFTER glide_set_acab and only adjusts the glad output variable, not the applied field - it is documented, not transcribed. (b) MassBalance - the surface/basal mass-balance application of add_surface_and_basal_mass_balance (libglissade/glissade_mass_balance.F90:819-1571) as the rate law d(thck)/dt = ifelse(thck <= 0 and net < 0, 0, net) with net = acab - bmlt (m/yr ice; bmlt = bmlt_ground + bmlt_float, 0 everywhere in the reference window): the RATE-LEVEL zeroing reproduces the Fortran's layer-by-layer removal that clips the column at zero (F90:1398-1419) without carrying a deficit into the next step (the Fortran's melt_potential accumulator is zeroed at the top of every mass_balance_driver call, F90:1096). The per-step melt_potential = max(0, -(H_pre + net_applied*dt)) of fully melted columns, the applied-rate bookkeeping acab_applied/bmlt_applied, and the tracer surface/bed handling are per-step ALGEBRAIC MAPS of the dumped entry state (the entry thickness H_pre and the entry tracers T1/Tbar/Tsurf/Tbed/T10), evaluated at the step start (time_span {0,0} in the tests): the layer-1 accumulation blend (H1*T1 + s*Tsurf)/(H1 + s) with H1 = sigma2*H_pre (new snow arrives at the current surface temperature temp(0), glissade_transport.F90:166), the layer-10 freeze-on blend (H10*T10 + b*Tbed)/(H10 + b) with H10 = (1 - sigma10)*H_pre (freeze-on arrives at the bed temperature, F90:172-174), and the column-mean law (H_pre*Tbar + s*T_surf_or_1 + b*Tbed)/(H_pre + s + b) as the nested application of the same cism_tracer_mix law (ablation removes the top layers at their own temperature, the layer-free form at the layer-1 temperature - exact while the ablation stays within layer 1; the Fortran's tracer = 0 of fully removed layers, F90:1411-1413, is the zero of fully melted columns); the ocean mask of glissade_get_masks (glissade_masks.F90:70-96) skips the application entirely in ice-free ocean cells (the same cism_ocean predicate); and the ice-age increment d(age)/dt = 1 where thck > 0 (glissade.F90:1203-1213) with age_usrf = 0 and age_lsrf = age (glissade_transport.F90:204-208) - the Fortran's age reset on ice-free cells is a documented difference for the stage-3 assembly. (c) SurfaceUpdate - the post-transport cleanup calc_lsrf_usrf (glimmer_utils.F90:344-378): lsrf = topg where grounded, lsrf = eus - (rhoi/rhoo)*thck where floating, usrf = lsrf + thck. The horizontal remapping and the first-order vertical remap are grid operations (one traced cell cannot pin them); their fingerprints are the documented advection residuals of the thickness and tracer pins."
 },
 "solver": {
  "stiffness": "low",
  "abstol": 1e-10,
  "reltol": 1e-6
 },
 "models": {
  "GladSmb": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./cism_templates.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "qsmb": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "surface mass balance from the cap (glad_inputs%qsmb, kg m-2 s-1 = mm s-1; the cism_cap.csv import column, accumulated over the mass-balance window)"
    },
    "tstep_mbal": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "h",
     "default": 8760.0,
     "description": "mass-balance accumulation window (params%tstep_mbal, hours; glad_main.F90:814-816). 8760 h = 1 yr in the reference run"
    },
    "hours2seconds": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s/h",
     "default": 3600.0,
     "description": "hours-to-seconds conversion factor (glad_constants.F90:44: hours2seconds = 3600)"
    },
    "rhow": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "default": 1000.0,
     "description": "fresh-water density (glimmer_physcon rhow = SHR_CONST_RHOFW = 1000 kg/m3; glimmer_physcon.F90:43,58)"
    },
    "rhoi": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "default": 917.0,
     "description": "ice density (glimmer_physcon rhoi = SHR_CONST_RHOICE = 917 kg/m3, glimmer_physcon.F90:41)"
    },
    "scyr": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s/yr",
     "default": 31536000.0,
     "description": "seconds per year of exactly 365 days (glimmer_physcon.F90:90: scyr = 31536000), the Fortran's year for the acab m/yr convention (glide_set_acab divides the m/yr input by scyr)"
    },
    "thck": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice thickness at the time of the glad step (glide_geometry%thck, m; the pre-step thickness used by the glad-level zeroing)"
    },
    "topg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "bedrock topography elevation (glide_geometry%topg, m)"
    },
    "eus": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "eustatic sea level (model%climate%eus, m; 0 in the reference run)"
    },
    "ocean": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "GLIDE_IS_OCEAN: the cism_ocean predicate on the pre-step thickness - bed below sea level and no ice (glide_mask.inc:33-34; the OCEAN bit of the thkmask is set where topg < eus, glide_set_geometry)"
    },
    "window_seconds": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "length of the mass-balance accumulation window in seconds = tstep_mbal*hours2seconds (the Fortran's accumulation factor of glad_main.F90:824)"
    },
    "windows_per_year": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "number of mass-balance windows per year = scyr/(tstep_mbal*hours2seconds), DERIVED from the named glad/glimmer constants (scyr, tstep_mbal, hours2seconds) rather than hand-set: the Fortran accumulates the window's SMB and passes the result to glide_set_acab as an m/yr rate (glad_main.F90:810-824, glad_timestep.F90:200), which is exact only when the window is 1 yr - the reference run has tstep_mbal = 8760 h = 1 yr, so windows_per_year = 1 and the per-window value equals the dump's m/yr ice column"
    },
    "acab_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "unmasked surface mass balance (m/yr ice; glad_main.F90:810-824, glad_timestep.F90:200): the Fortran chain qsmb*tstep_mbal*hours2seconds/rhow*rhow/rhoi*windows_per_year - qsmb*tstep_mbal*hours2seconds is the kg/m2 of water over the window, /rhow is the mm-to-m depth conversion of the Fortran's /1000 (a kg/m2 water column is mm of water), *rhow/rhoi converts water-equivalent to ice (glad_timestep.F90:200), and *windows_per_year turns the per-window accumulation into the per-year rate of the dump column (the rhow factors cancel, which is why the Fortran's own chain reduces to qsmb*tstep_mbal*3600/rhoi in the reference run)"
    },
    "acab": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "the surface mass balance as applied to the ice sheet (m/yr ice; model%climate%acab after the glad-level zeroing of glad_timestep.F90:171-187 and the m/yr conversion of glide_set_acab)"
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "ocean",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "cism_ocean",
      "bindings": {
       "thck": "thck",
       "topg": "topg",
       "eus": "eus"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "window_seconds",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "tstep_mbal",
       "hours2seconds"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "windows_per_year",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "scyr",
       "window_seconds"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "acab_raw",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "qsmb",
             "rhow"
            ]
           },
           "tstep_mbal"
          ]
         },
         "hours2seconds"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "rhow",
           "rhoi"
          ]
         },
         "windows_per_year"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "acab",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "==",
        "args": [
         "ocean",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "m/yr"
       },
       {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "and",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "<=",
            "args": [
             "thck",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 0.0,
              "units": "m"
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "<",
            "args": [
             "acab_raw",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 0.0,
              "units": "m/yr"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.0,
          "units": "m/yr"
         },
         "acab_raw"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "qsmb_to_acab_step1_cell2511",
     "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 1, cell 25,11): qsmb = 4.05302216536369290e-06 kg/m2/s, tstep_mbal = 8760 h give the Fortran chain acab_raw = qsmb*8760*3600/1000*1000/917*1 = 0.13938506761931235 m/yr ice (windows_per_year = scyr/(8760*3600) = 1), identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab of the same cell at step 1 (rel 0.0e+00 on all 64 traced cells, see README-cism-transport.md). thck = 1.30004894733428955 m > 0, so no zeroing fires and acab = acab_raw.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsmb": 4.05302216536369290e-06,
      "thck": 1.30004894733428955,
      "topg": 1082.0
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "acab_raw",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 0.13938506761931235,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "acab",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 0.13938506761931235,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "ocean",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 0.0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "qsmb_to_acab_cap2_cell2511",
     "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 2, cell 25,11): qsmb = -1.69074734385490992e-05 kg/m2/s gives acab = -0.58145483354207683 m/yr ice, identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab of the same cell at step 3 (the ablation year). thck = 1.4394647029325882 m > 0, so the ice-free zeroing does not fire.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsmb": -1.69074734385490992e-05,
      "thck": 1.4394647029325882,
      "topg": 1082.0
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "acab",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": -0.58145483354207683,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "qsmb_to_acab_step1_cell2611",
     "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 1, cell 26,11): the largest traced accumulation qsmb = 6.05103156348133181e-05 kg/m2/s gives acab = 2.0809741699667099 m/yr ice, identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab (step 1).",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsmb": 6.05103156348133181e-05,
      "thck": 14.0,
      "topg": 1752.9000244140625
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "acab",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 2.0809741699667099,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "zeroing_icefree_ablation_cell2811_step2",
     "description": "Dump pin of the glad-level ice-free zeroing (glad_timestep.F90:171-175): the cism_transport.csv entry row of cell 28,11 at step 2 has thck = 0 exactly (the step-1 SMB melted the 0.0199585 m column out) and the dump's acab column reads 0 - the raw cap value for cap_step 1 (qsmb = -2.05729925935643034e-05 kg/m2/s, i.e. acab_raw = -0.7075135162820545 m/yr ice) is zeroed because thck <= 0 and acab_raw < 0. The acab_raw assertion pins the raw value; the acab = 0 assertion pins the zeroing.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsmb": -2.05729925935643034e-05,
      "thck": 0.0,
      "topg": 921.1400146484375
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "acab_raw",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": -0.7075135162820545,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "acab",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 0.0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "thin_ice_no_zeroing_cell2811_step3",
     "description": "Dump pin of the zeroing branch boundary: the cism_transport.csv entry row of cell 28,11 at step 3 has thck = 1.6503583323323985e-05 m > 0 (thin ice advected in during step 2) and the dump's acab column reads -1.7674468845051972 m/yr ice - the raw cap_step-2 value (qsmb = -5.13936070868615494e-05 kg/m2/s), NOT zeroed: the glad-level condition thck <= 0 fails for any ice at all, however thin.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsmb": -5.13936070868615494e-05,
      "thck": 1.6503583323323985e-05,
      "topg": 921.1400146484375
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "acab",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": -1.7674468845051972,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "MassBalance": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./cism_templates.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "acab": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "surface mass balance (m/yr ice), as zeroed by GladSmb (model%climate%acab, m/s in the Fortran; glad_timestep.F90:171-187)"
    },
    "bmlt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "basal melt rate bmlt_ground + bmlt_float (m/yr ice; positive melting, negative freeze-on; model%basal_melt%bmlt, glissade_apply_smb F90:842-850). 0 everywhere in the reference window (cold base, no shelf melt), so the bmlt branches are unpinned source formulas (see README-cism-transport.md)"
    },
    "topg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "bedrock topography elevation (m), for the ocean mask"
    },
    "eus": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "eustatic sea level (m; 0 in the reference run)"
    },
    "dt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "yr",
     "default": 0.5,
     "description": "dynamics time step (model%numerics%dt, yr; 0.5 yr in the reference run: two dynamics steps per cap year)"
    },
    "x_sigma2": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "normalized level of the layer-1 interface: x = (up-1)/(upn-1) = 1/10 for upn = 11 (glide_setup.F90:303-308)"
    },
    "x_sigma10": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.9,
     "description": "normalized level of the layer-10 interface: x = 9/10 for upn = 11"
    },
    "n_sigma": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 2.0,
     "description": "SIGMA_COMPUTE_GLIDE stretch exponent n = 2 (glide_setup.F90:303-308)"
    },
    "H_pre": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step ice thickness (m; the dumped entry thck of the step, the thickness the Fortran's layer loops start from, F90:1330-1332: thck_layer = thck*(sigma(k+1)-sigma(k))). The tracer blends, the applied-rate bookkeeping and melt_potential are per-step algebraic maps of this entry state, evaluated at the step start"
    },
    "T1": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step layer-1 temperature (model%temper%temp(1,:,:), degC)"
    },
    "Tbar": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step column-mean temperature over layers 1..10 (the layer-free representation of the temperature tracer column; not a Fortran state - the dump's exit mean is derived)"
    },
    "Tsurf": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "upper-surface temperature temp(0), the temperature of new accumulation (tracers_usrf of the temperature tracer, glissade_transport.F90:166)"
    },
    "Tbed": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "lower-surface temperature temp(upn), the temperature of basal freeze-on (tracers_lsrf, glissade_transport.F90:172-174)"
    },
    "T10": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step layer-10 temperature (model%temper%temp(10,:,:), degC)"
    },
    "sigma2": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "glide sigma level 2 = glide_calc_sigma(0.1, 2) = 0.23140495867768607 (glide_setup.F90:380-387); the layer-1 thickness fraction"
    },
    "sigma10": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "glide sigma level 10 = glide_calc_sigma(0.9, 2) = 0.96398891966759004; the layer-10 thickness fraction is 1 - sigma10"
    },
    "ocean_mask": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ocean mask of the mass-balance driver: the cism_ocean predicate on the ENTRY thickness (topg < eus and H_pre <= 0; glissade_get_masks, glissade_masks.F90:70-96, computed from the pre-step state). The SMB and BMB are not applied to ocean cells (glissade_mass_balance.F90:1333-1341) and their applied rates and melt_potential stay 0 (the effective_areafrac = 0 of ocean cells, F90:893-901). No traced cell is ocean (all 32 cells have topg >= 921 m): source formula, unpinned"
    },
    "net": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "unmasked net mass balance acab - bmlt (m/yr ice)"
    },
    "net_applied": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "net mass balance actually applied: 0 in ocean cells, else net (the Fortran's ocean_mask guard, F90:1333-1341, and the effective_areafrac = 0 of ocean cells, F90:893-901)"
    },
    "thck": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice thickness (m; glide_geometry%thck after the SMB application). The ODE state of the rate law d(thck)/dt = ifelse(thck <= 0 and net_applied < 0, 0, net_applied): the rate-level guard reproduces the Fortran's layer-by-layer removal that clips the column at zero (F90:1398-1419) while never carrying a negative thickness - and its deficit - into the next step (the Fortran re-derives thck from the clipped layers every step; the state-level max(0, thck_raw) of the first review round could not express the per-step zeroing and was replaced by the guard). The guard is discontinuous at the clip, so the diffsol BDF arm of the runner freezes the state at its first negative step; the document's declared solver tolerances (abstol 1e-10, reltol 1e-6) keep that landing within ~1e-9 m, covered by the abs tolerances of the full-melt pins"
    },
    "H_post": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "end-of-step thickness H_pre + net_applied*dt (m), the per-step algebraic image of the entry state: the pre-clip thickness the Fortran's layer loops produce (the layer-free continuous limit is exact at step boundaries for the constant-net dump steps). H_post <= 0 marks the fully melted columns (tracers zeroed, melt_potential > 0)"
    },
    "melt_potential": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "total thickness (m) of additional ice that could have been melted by the available acab/bmlt in columns that melted out completely: max(0, -H_post) (derived, not a dump column). The Fortran's per-step melt_potential accumulator (F90:1418-1422, 1452-1457) is zeroed at the top of every mass_balance_driver call (F90:1096) - it is a per-step diagnostic, not a model state - so the esm form is the algebraic map of the entry state, which is what the tests pin"
    },
    "s": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "signed surface thickness change per step (m): acab*dt; positive accumulation, negative ablation"
    },
    "b": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "freeze-on thickness per step (m): -bmlt*dt for bmlt < 0, else 0 (bed_accum, F90:1455-1456)"
    },
    "H1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step layer-1 thickness = sigma2*H_pre (thck_layer(:,:,1), F90:1330-1332)"
    },
    "H10": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "pre-step layer-10 thickness = (1 - sigma10)*H_pre"
    },
    "acab_applied": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "surface mass balance actually applied (m/yr ice; model%climate%acab_applied, m/s in the Fortran): the full acab while the column survives, -H_pre/dt when the ablation removes the whole column (F90:1385-1422; the Fortran accumulates the applied amount in m per step and converts back to m/s at F90:1567). Derived (not a dump column) - the dump carries the input acab, not the applied value; pinned from the source formula at the full-melt pins"
    },
    "bmlt_applied": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "basal melt rate actually applied (m/yr ice; model%basal_melt%bmlt_applied): the full bmlt for freeze-on and for basal melt while the column survives, the remaining column thickness per step when the melt removes it all (F90:1437-1457). Derived (not a dump column); unpinned (bmlt = 0 in the reference window, see README-cism-transport.md)"
    },
    "T1_out": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "layer-1 temperature after the SMB application (the dump's exit temp_001): the accumulation blend (H1*T1 + s*Tsurf)/(H1 + s) of F90:1380-1386 (new ice arrives at the surface temperature), unchanged by ablation while the ablation stays within layer 1 (F90:1398-1413 removes ice without changing the tracer; the layer-free model keeps T1 once the ablated depth exceeds H1 - the layer-2 identity is lost, a documented approximation), and 0 in fully melted columns (the tracer = 0 of F90:1411-1413; the dump's exit temp_001 of the melted cells reads 0 exactly)"
    },
    "Tbar_blend": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "column-mean temperature after the surface term of the step: the cism_tracer_mix law (H_pre*Tbar + s*T_in)/(H_pre + s) with T_in = Tsurf for accumulation (s > 0) and T_in = T1 for ablation (the layer-free form removes the ablated ice at the layer-1 temperature, exact while the ablation stays within layer 1). The basal freeze-on term of the mean law is applied on top by Tbar_out (the mixing law composes: mass times tracer is conserved step by step)"
    },
    "Tbar_out": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "column-mean temperature after the SMB application (derived, not a dump column - the Fortran has no column-mean state): the nested cism_tracer_mix law (H_pre*Tbar + s*T_in + b*Tbed)/(H_pre + s + b), i.e. the surface blend of Tbar_blend followed by the freeze-on blend at the bed temperature (mass x tracer conservation of the Fortran's layer updates), 0 in fully melted columns. Unpinned: on the window's only ablation cells the law's effect (4.7e-4 / 3.8e-5 relative) lies inside the advection-dominated tolerance, so no assertion could fail - see README-cism-transport.md"
    },
    "T10_out": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "degC",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "layer-10 temperature after the SMB application (the dump's exit temp_010): the freeze-on blend (H10*T10 + b*Tbed)/(H10 + b) of F90:1458-1465 (freeze-on arrives at the bed temperature), unchanged otherwise, 0 in fully melted columns. Unpinned (bmlt = 0 in the reference window)"
    },
    "age": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice age (yr; model%geometry%ice_age, seconds internally, converted to years on output). Incremented d(age)/dt = 1 where thck > 0 (glissade.F90:1203-1213). The Fortran additionally RESETS the age to 0 on ice-free cells (F90:1209-1213); the ODE form only stops the increment - the reset is unobservable in the reference window (no traced cell refreezes) and is a documented difference for the stage-3 assembly. Unpinned (no age column in the dump, and the reference window never refreezes - see README-cism-transport.md)"
    },
    "age_usrf": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice age of new surface accumulation = 0 (tracers_usrf of the age tracer, glissade_transport.F90:204-206). Unpinned"
    },
    "age_lsrf": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "yr",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice age of basal freeze-on = the bottom-layer age (tracers_lsrf, glissade_transport.F90:207-208); the layer-free model's bottom-layer age is the age state. Unpinned"
    }
   },
