    {
     "id": "full_melt_step1_cell2811",
     "description": "Dump pin of the full-melt clip through the rate-level guard: cell 28,11 at step 1 has entry thck = 0.019958499819040298 m with acab = -0.7075135162820545 m/yr (the zeroing did not fire: thck > 0). One 0.5-yr step would remove 0.35375675814102725 m - the whole column and more - so d(thck)/dt = net while thck > 0 and 0 once the column is gone: the exit thck is clipped to 0 (dump exit thck = 0 exactly). The rate guard is discontinuous at the crossing, and the diffsol BDF arm of the runner freezes the state at its first negative step; under the document's declared solver tolerances (abstol 1e-10, reltol 1e-6) that landing is within ~1e-9 m of 0, covered by the abs tolerance (1e-8, still eight orders below the -0.354 m the unguarded law would give). The per-step melt_potential, the applied rates and the tracer zeroing of the same row are pinned in the full_melt_step1_cell2811_rates algebraic test.",
